[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":93},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":26},"tipo","metodo","cubo",{"_11":91,"_13":91,"_28":92},"id","ortega","nome","Ortega","nomeLongo","Face, OLL and PBL (or Varasano)","termo",{"_28":88,"_89":90},"niveis",[49],"introducao","<p>A first fast method: build just the bottom face (without caring about the sides), orient the top one (<a href=\"/en/glossary#ortega\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).\">Ortega</a> <a href=\"/en/glossary#oll\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Makes the top face all one color, without caring about the position of the pieces. There are 57 cases; in 2-Look OLL, 10 cases in two parts.\">OLL</a>, 7 cases) and permute both layers at once (Ortega <a href=\"/en/glossary#pbl\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"On the 2x2 (Ortega): puts the pieces of both layers in place at once.\">PBL</a>, 6 cases).</p>\n","etapas",[32,33,34],"historias",[27],{"_13":14,"_28":29,"_30":31},"endereco","/historia#ortega","resumo","The method is named after Victor Ortega, who spread it (in 2001 it went up on Josef Jelinek's site), but the idea is older: it comes from a corners-first 3x3 method, published by Jeffrey Varasano in 1981, which is why it is also called the Varasano method.",{"_11":81,"_13":82,"_37":83,"_39":84,"_41":85,"_42":-7,"_44":86},{"_11":63,"_13":64,"_37":65,"_39":66,"_41":-7,"_42":67,"_44":68},{"_11":35,"_13":36,"_37":38,"_39":40,"_41":-7,"_42":43,"_44":45},"pbl","PBL","html","<p>Both faces are done: the corners just need swapping until the sides match. Look at each layer: a side with both colors matching (a &quot;<a href=\"/en/glossary#par\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"A corner and an edge that go together into the same slot in F2L.\">pair</a>&quot;) means an adjacent swap (<em>Adj</em>); no pair, a diagonal swap (<em>Opp</em>). A layer that is already right has a pair on all 4 sides. The 6 cases are the combinations of the two layers; if only the bottom one is wrong, turn the cube over (<code>x2</code>) and it goes to the top. At the end, a <code>U</code> or <code>D</code> turn finishes it.</p>\n","grupos",[46],"pagina","treino","/2x2/treino?grupo=ortega-pbl","imagem","/imagens/diagramas/02b6a512b5070e6c.svg",{"_11":47,"_13":47,"_48":49,"_50":51,"_52":53,"_54":55,"_28":56},"Ortega PBL","nivel","iniciante","casos",6,"conjunto",false,"ids",[57,58,59,60,61,62],"/2x2/ortega-pbl","2X2-PBL-Adj","2X2-PBL-Opp","2X2-PBL-OppOpp","2X2-PBL-AdjAdj","2X2-PBL-AdjOpp","2X2-PBL-OppAdj","oll","OLL","<p>With white on the bottom, make the top face all yellow. Look at how many yellow stickers are already on top and where the others are, on the sides: there are 7 cases, the same shapes as the corners of the 3x3 <a href=\"/en/glossary#oll\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Makes the top face all one color, without caring about the position of the pieces. There are 57 cases; in 2-Look OLL, 10 cases in two parts.\">OLL</a> (<a href=\"/en/glossary#sune\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Two short OLL algorithms that orient 3 corners: R U R' U R U2 R' (Sune) and R U2 R' U' R U' R' (Anti-Sune).\">Sune</a>, AntiSune, H, Pi, P, T and L).</p>\n",[69],"/2x2/treino?grupo=ortega-oll","/imagens/diagramas/085c13cc78086489.svg",{"_11":70,"_13":70,"_48":49,"_50":71,"_52":53,"_54":72,"_28":73},"Ortega OLL",7,[74,75,76,77,78,79,80],"/2x2/ortega-oll","2X2-OLL-Sune","2X2-OLL-AntiSune","2X2-OLL-Pi","2X2-OLL-P","2X2-OLL-L","2X2-OLL-T","2X2-OLL-H","primeira-face","1st face","<p>The white face on the bottom, with the <a href=\"/en/glossary#sexy-move\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The trigger R U R' U', the most common of all.\">sexy move</a> <code>R U R&#39; U&#39;</code>. The sides may end up swapped.</p>\n",[],{"_13":82,"_28":87},"/imagens/diagramas/9e280cd467752f31.svg","/2x2/primeira-face","/en/glossary#ortega","dica","A 2x2 method: it builds one face, orients the top one (Ortega OLL) and permutes both layers at once (PBL).","2x2","/2x2/",{"_94":95,"_96":97},"cubos",[100,101,102,103,104,105,106],"idiomas",[98,99],"pt","en",{"_11":115,"_13":115},{"_11":91,"_13":91},{"_11":114,"_13":114},{"_11":113,"_13":113},{"_11":111,"_13":112},{"_11":109,"_13":110},{"_11":107,"_13":108},"skewb","Skewb","pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","3x3"]
